Modelica source:
```modelica
connector Flange
  Real phi;
  flow Real tau;
end Flange;
model Gear
  Flange support;
  Flange flange_a;
  Flange flange_b;
end Gear;
model Drive
  Flange support;
  Flange flange;
end Drive;
model Fixed
  Flange flange;
end Fixed;
model Study
  Flange boundary;
  Gear gear;
  Drive torque;
  Fixed fixed;
equation
  connect(gear.support, fixed.flange);
  connect(torque.support, fixed.flange);
  connect(boundary, torque.support);
end Study;
```

Question:
Within the equation scope of model instance Study, return the canonical signed member vector for the primitive flow connection set formed by explicit connect statements in that scope that contains boundary.tau.

Target:
boundary.tau

Answer format:
Use ascending path:integer entries joined by commas without spaces; coefficients must be primitive, nonzero, and oriented so the first coefficient is positive.
Return exactly {"answer":"..."}.
